Subject: [PATCH 6/7] radv/ps5: narrower waits between draws, late allocation and shader culling switches (lot 57)

RADV_DEBUG=syncshaders keeps the title's GPU hangs away on the console: every
draw waits for the pixel shaders of the one before (PS_PARTIAL_FLUSH and
PFP_SYNC_ME), so each pays its whole latency alone. Three switches, all unset:
as before; none changes a compiled shader or the shader cache's key.

- RADV_PS5_SYNC_PS: 1 or each as before; program waits only before a draw whose
  shaders are not the last draw's, a command buffer's first draw and a dispatch,
  when a draw ran since the last wait for the pixel shaders (or a colour or depth
  flush); vertex puts VS_PARTIAL_FLUSH after every draw.
- RADV_PS5_LATE_ALLOC: gfx10 gives NGG and vertex waves GFX10's late allocation
  (at most 64, CU2 and CU3 out of their mask, which ac_compute_late_alloc says
  prevents a hardware deadlock there) instead of GFX10.3's; off gives none.
- RADV_PS5_NGGC=0: the NGG shader culling off at draw time (settings register 0);
  GFX10's hang with 100% culling is not in this GPU's description.

radv_ps5_waits_stats and radv_ps5_waits_settings (radv_ps5_waits.h) give the title
the counts of draws and waits and the switches as read, for its log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

